I have gathered all the requested information. Here is my thorough report.

## Overview

The repository at `/home/daniel/sandbox` is a Spring PetClinic REST app with a parallel OfficeFloor implementation. Owner creation via REST is driven by a YAML "flow" file (`owners.POST.yml`) that chains together small single-responsibility Java "function" classes. DTOs (`OwnerFieldsDto`, `OwnerDto`, `OwnerPageDto`) are code-generated from `openapi.yml` at build time (no hand-written source files exist for them).

---

## 1. The POST owners YAML

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`

```yaml
composition:
  authorize: "hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')"

validate:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.ValidateOwnerRequiredFields
  next: normalizeTelephone

normalizeTelephone:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.NormalizeOwnerTelephone
  next: build

build:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.BuildOwner
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: save

save:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.SaveOwner
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: respond

respond:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.RespondWithOwnerCreated
  govern: [ transaction ]
```

The create chain is: `ValidateOwnerRequiredFields` → `NormalizeOwnerTelephone` → `BuildOwner` → `SaveOwner` → `RespondWithOwnerCreated`. First step requires role `OWNER_ADMIN`.

---

## 2. Java function classes referenced by the YAML

All under `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/`.

`ValidateOwnerRequiredFields.java` — binds the request body (without `@Valid`), collects blank/missing required fields, throws `MissingOwnerFieldsException`, and republishes the body via `Out<OwnerFieldsDto>` for downstream steps. It is the only step that binds the body.

```java
public class ValidateOwnerRequiredFields {
    public void service(@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto request, Out<OwnerFieldsDto> validated)
            throws MissingOwnerFieldsException {
        List<String> missing = new ArrayList<>();
        if (isBlank(request.getFirstName())) { missing.add("firstName"); }
        if (isBlank(request.getLastName()))  { missing.add("lastName"); }
        if (isBlank(request.getAddress()))   { missing.add("address"); }
        if (isBlank(request.getCity()))      { missing.add("city"); }
        if (isBlank(request.getTelephone())) { missing.add("telephone"); }
        if (!missing.isEmpty()) { throw new MissingOwnerFieldsException(missing); }
        validated.set(request);
    }
    private static boolean isBlank(String value) { return value == null || value.isBlank(); }
}
```

`NormalizeOwnerTelephone.java` — strips all non-digits from telephone, requires exactly 10 digits, mutates the DTO in place, else throws `InvalidTelephoneException`.

```java
public class NormalizeOwnerTelephone {
    public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request) throws InvalidTelephoneException {
        String telephone = request.getTelephone();
        String digits = telephone == null ? "" : telephone.replaceAll("\\D", "");
        if (digits.length() != 10) { throw new InvalidTelephoneException(telephone); }
        request.setTelephone(digits);
    }
}
```

`BuildOwner.java` — maps the validated DTO to an `Owner` entity via MapStruct `OwnerMapper.toOwner(...)`, publishes as `Out<Owner> built`.

```java
public class BuildOwner {
    public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerMapper ownerMapper, Out<Owner> built) {
        built.set(ownerMapper.toOwner(request));
    }
}
```

`SaveOwner.java` — persists via `OwnerRepository.save(owner)`.

```java
public class SaveOwner {
    public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
        ownerRepository.save(owner);
    }
}
```

`RespondWithOwnerCreated.java` — maps entity back to `OwnerDto`, returns `201 Created` with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.

```java
public class RespondWithOwnerCreated {
    public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerMapper ownerMapper,
            ObjectResponse<ResponseEntity<OwnerDto>> response) {
        OwnerDto dto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
        response.send(ResponseEntity.created(URI.create("/api/owners/" + owner.getId())).body(dto));
    }
}
```

Related helper functions in the same package (not in the POST chain but relevant): `ValidateOwner.java` (a `@Validated`/`@Valid` variant used before load on update paths), `ApplyOwner.java` (copies DTO fields onto an existing `Owner`, used by the PUT/update flow), plus `LoadOwner`, `ListOwners`, `ListOwnersPage`, `DeleteOwner`, `RespondWithOwner`, `RespondWithOwnerUpdated`, `BuildOwnersPet`, `LoadOwnersPet`.

`ApplyOwner.java` (used on update, mirrors the field set):
```java
public class ApplyOwner {
    public void service(@Val Owner owner, @Val OwnerFieldsDto request) {
        owner.setAddress(request.getAddress());
        owner.setCity(request.getCity());
        owner.setFirstName(request.getFirstName());
        owner.setLastName(request.getLastName());
        owner.setTelephone(request.getTelephone());
    }
}
```

---

## 3. Owner entity and OwnerRepository

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` — JPA `@Entity` mapped to table `owners`, extends `Person` (which holds `firstName`/`lastName`). Key fields:

```java
@Entity
